From: Jules <jules@example.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2025 15:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix incorrect log file path in webapp

The /logs route in app.py was attempting to read from 'logs.log'
instead of the correctly configured 'logs/app.log'.

This patch corrects the hardcoded file path to allow the page
to load without crashing. A more robust solution would involve
reading the path from config.ini.
---
 app.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app.py b/app.py
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/app.py
+++ b/app.py
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 @app.route('/logs')
 def logs():
     # Read and display logs from the log file
-    with open('logs.log', 'r') as log_file:
+    with open('logs/app.log', 'r') as log_file:
         logs = log_file.readlines()
     return render_template('logs.html', logs=logs)

